findings.detail:
At 1x1 in-plane the donor sheet is about 2.8e14 cm^-2, roughly 1000 times the channel densities, and W/(W+In) = 1/56 = 1.8 %. Read only local quantities inside one run:
- the W-5d level relative to the host CB (the lowest band with W weight below 3 %);
- the W-O bonds;
- the W-5d Löwdin weight.
The mass of a degenerately filled band is not the TCAD mass, because of band filling and the non-parabolicity alpha = 0.55-0.63 1/eV. Fit the host band, not the occupied W-derived band. The electron count is odd (1329), and the bulk moments of 0.6-0.7 muB did not meet the non-magnetic criterion, so a spin-polarized check is needed. dat2h5.py handles only nspin=1, so a GPU spin-polarized run would lose its planar average. The most valuable question this item answers is donor depth versus thickness: in bulk E_F lies in W-5d/CB states, at 1 nm the W level is 0.19 eV below the host CB. Confinement-induced donor deactivation would give a physical basis to the fitted Nd_eff(t) law. Pre-register the comparison of E(W level) - E(host CB) at 1 and 2 nm, using the same in-plane cell.

PAW exact exchange is unusable in the QE 7.3.1 GPU build, and SG15 sets exist locally only for In, O, H and W.
Do:
- bulk and 1 nm (done; read the edge shifts out of the existing runs);
- bulk W24d with 80 atoms;
- bulk V_O^q single points;
- bulk mass with zero-weight k-points.
Do not:
- the 2 nm slab (exact-exchange arrays about 136 GB, estimate);
- the W or V_O slabs;
- any Pd or Al system: no SG15 files, and exact exchange for metals needs dense q sampling and is infeasible at this size.
Apply HSE as ratios or edge shifts to the PAW-PBE results, never as absolute NC values; the NC-PAW dEg offset is 1.6 %. Runs over about 25 h cannot write EOS checkpoints, and the snapshot loop copies only text outputs, so a long HSE job cannot restart from its wavefunctions.

(1) Dipole correction: pw_input writes a fixed &CONTROL block and has only an extra_sys hook in &SYSTEM. Add tefield/dipfield in &CONTROL and edir/emaxpos/eopreg/eamp in &SYSTEM. Teach analyze_slabs.py to read two different vacuum levels; the planar potential of a pp.x plot_num=11 run then includes the sawtooth. (2) Extend dat2h5.py to nspin=2. (3) Set memory floors for cells above 176 atoms: the final SCF used about 2x the memory of the relaxation (66 vs 31 GB). (4) Pre-register criteria for each new item, for example:
- Phi_B changes by less than 0.05 eV between 5 and 7 Pd layers;
- E_seg changes by less than 0.05 eV between 1x1 and 2x1;
- the interior macroscopic average is flat within ±20 meV;
- HSE ratios are reproduced within 0.02 under reduced settings.
